# KNOWN GAP (`todo/t0704`) — 🚨 CAPTURING A COLLECTION IN A CLOSURE AND THEN
# REALLOCATING IT is a use-after-free. rc 139 SIGSEGV on BOTH backends.
#
#     String() f = (): v.get(0).unwrap()   # closure captures `v`
#     while i < 64: v.push(mk(...))        # source realloc'd through `v`
#     print(f())                           # reads freed memory -> rc 139
#
# MECHANISM — THE CAPTURE BOUNDARY. A closure's captured collection handle is a
# BORROW BOUND AT CAPTURE TIME (`src/ir/lowering/closures.rs`, the
# `CaptureMode::ByValue` arm: `field_load` -> `Ptr(cap.type_id)` +
# `set_field_borrow`), and a realloc of the source leaves that handle stale. The
# rescue owed is at the capture boundary — a closure capture is an ownership
# boundary per AGENTS.md § Ownership at Consuming Positions — not in the
# mutation prescan.
#
# ⚠ AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS HEADER BLAMED A MISSING `Expr::Closure` ARM IN
# `cow_after_expr_moves` AND A `_ => {}` CATCH-ALL. That diagnosis is RETRACTED:
# the arm EXISTS and the match is exhaustive over every `Expr` variant, and this
# repro still segfaults. It is not a prescan defect. Do NOT start there.
#
# THE DISCRIMINATOR IS THE CAPTURE ROOT, NOT WHERE THE MUTATION IS SPELLED —
# measured, both backends, both before and after the per-function-prescan
# centralisation that fixed the sibling non-capture shapes:
#
#   | shape                                              | capture | result   |
#   |----------------------------------------------------|---------|----------|
#   | this file — mutate OUTSIDE the closure              | yes     | rc 139   |
#   | `closure_capture_inside_body_uaf.gg` — INSIDE       | yes     | rc 139   |
#   | same body, vector LOCAL to the closure             | no      | rc 0 ✅  |
#   | capture + 0 pushes (control)                        | yes     | rc 0     |
#   | capture + 1 push (control)                          | yes     | rc 0     |
#
# The last two controls are why the REALLOC is load-bearing, and the third row
# is the live regression fixture `cow_closure_body_view_survives_realloc.gg` —
# the same statements without a capture are now correct. So capture is
# NECESSARY; the sibling repro (no saved view variable at all) shows it is also
# SUFFICIENT, which rules out "a CoW view taken inside the body that the prescan
# failed to materialize".
#
# ⚠ THE REALLOC IS LOAD-BEARING (64 pushes, not one) and the payload must be
# heap-FORCED via `mk`, never a literal. One push is rc 0 and proves nothing.
#
# Family, stated so this is not merged with either sibling:
#   * `t0699` — a user &self MUTATOR METHOD's NAME is absent from the
#     `MUTATING_METHODS` list, so the prescan never fires. Wrong KEY -> right
#     set. Fixed by the typed-mutator fix.
#   * `t0703` — the view is spelled through an ALIAS name, so `CollectionId`
#     names the spelling instead of the storage owner. Right key -> wrong SET.
#     Fixed by the alias-root fix.
#   * THIS — neither: the capture binds a borrow that a later realloc severs.
#
# ⇒ Bears on DEEP-1 (`t0543`): closure capture is a rest position the lazy-bind
# model must materialize at, and obligation (ii) is already unsound here.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints `hello`, both backends, ASan-clean.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(mk("hel", "lo"))
    String() f = (): v.get(0).unwrap()
    int i = 0
    while i < 64:
        v.push(mk("fill", "er"))
        i = i + 1
    print(f())
